# Working in LLMZ80

The full guide is CONTRIBUTING.md. This is the short version, and the parts an
assistant gets wrong without it.

## What this project is

Studio (`llmz80/studio/`) takes one sentence describing a game, designs it,
draws its art, writes C for a ZX Spectrum or Amstrad CPC, builds it with the
machine's real toolchain, and then boots the binary in ZEsarUX, presses keys at
it and reads the running program's memory to check it behaved as designed.

The model is **Anthropic's**, called through `llmz80/studio/llm.py`, named in
`config.yml`. There is no OpenAI client, no Qdrant, no embeddings and no RAG
stack: all of that belonged to `llm_z80.py`, the single-file generator Studio
replaced, and it was deleted. Do not reintroduce it, and do not describe the
project in those terms.

Retrieval is a local, deterministic catalogue (`core/example_catalog.py`) over
`examples/`. No vectors, no service to start.

## Hard rules

- **English everywhere** in code, comments, commit messages and anything the
  interface prints. Linguistic data is the exception: Spanish stopwords in
  `core/example_catalog.py`, bilingual colour and comparison words in
  `studio/palette.py` and `studio/runtime_exam.py`, and the deliberately
  bilingual `benchmarks/prompts.yml`. A design's own prose is in whatever
  language it was briefed in; `Metadata.language` defaults to `es`.
- **Write the failing test first**, and run it red before writing the fix.
- **Comments say why**, citing the run that taught it — which program broke,
  what it reported, what was tried first. Never restate what the code does.
- **Type everything.** mypy runs with `disallow_untyped_defs` and the tree is
  clean. `object` as a parameter type means unchecked; write a `Protocol`.
- **`make quality-gate` before pushing.** flake8, black, isort, mypy and bandit
  all fail CI; none of them are advisory.
- Line length 100. `make format` is isort then black.

## Two invariants worth understanding

**The design is a document, not a prompt.** `studio/models.py` schema v4 lets a
design name its own tiles, entities, mechanics and observables. There is no
genre enum and no fixed vocabulary, on purpose. Adding one is the mistake v4
exists to prevent.

**A gate measures or it abstains.** Every gate answers `True`, `False` or
`None`. `None` is never a pass. On the Amstrad CPC the pacing and attribute
gates abstain for reasons about the machine (no free-running frame counter with
the firmware disabled; no attribute area to judge), while acceptance, animation
and the state probe really do watch.

## Layout

    llmz80/studio/    the pipeline: design, art, codegen, build, gates
    llmz80/core/      the state contract, toolchain discovery, the catalogue
    llmz80/quality/   ZEsarUX over ZRCP, for both machines
    resources/studio_lib/        platform.h and one platform.c per machine
    resources/studio_reference/  a complete game per machine, to prove the gates
    examples/         compiling programs, for retrieval
